[align=center][b][size=26]The [color=#475577]Eyebrow[/color]maxxing Guide [/size]
 [font=Arial][size=18]how to get... ideal eyebrows[/size][/font]
 [size=9][i][color=#b8312f].[/color][/i][/size][/b][/align]

 Eyebrows are often neglected and undervalued, but they can affect your looks vastly just like haircuts do. In this thread I am going to introduce you to my perception of ideal eyebrows and the importance of them, elobrate the reasons behind it and also explain how to groom them properly.  [i]If you have little to no eyebrow growth[/i] - do not worry, because I will cover this issue later in this thread.

 [size=22][b]The [color=#475577]Importance[/color][/b][/size]

[align=center][/align]

 Eyebrows have many reasons why there are so crucial. On the one hand there are [b]evolutionary reasons[/b], which I will elobrate later, on the other hand they are [b]needed to recognize people[/b] and seperate them from eachother. People would have a hard time recognizing you if you'd shave them off completely. The same wouldn't occur, if you would get rid of your lashes or get jaw fillers for example. Therefore we can come to the conclusion that even [u]the slightest change of your eyebrows will have a great impact on your looks and how people percieve you.[/u]

 [size=22][b]The [color=#475577]Shape[/color][/b][/size]

[align=center][img alt="Jayv" width=200 height=150]https://i.looksmax.org/attachments/2018/12/1417785_Jayv.gif[/img]
[/align]

 There are various eyebrow shapes and each of them has a different impact on your face. Most guides I have seen advise you to pick a shape based on your face shape. In my opinion however; [b]flat eyebrows are the most ideal[/b] for men, [u]no matter what your face shape looks like[/u]. You want your eye area to be [b]as compact and hunter-like as possible[/b], as this gets percieved as an alpha trait. So having round shaped eyebrows for instance, will make you look worse.

 Here's me with round and flat eyebrows. I've had posted it before:

[align=center][/align]

 [size=22][b]The [color=#475577]Thickness[/color][/b][/size]

[align=center][/align]

 The thickness itself is very important, because of the same evolutionary reasons why a prominent brow bone or a highset cheekbone is important for males. All of them were meant to protect the eyes while hunting or fighting. (Not only the thickness of the eyebrows, but also the length, set and density) Hence they [b]should be thick[/b], but there's still a limit.

 [size=22][b]The [color=#475577]Outer Length[/color][/b][/size]

 Your eyebrows should [u]at least[/u] reach the outer part of your eyelids. I found that they look better if they're longer than that ([b]reaching your cheekbones or going a little further[/b]), since horizontal length of your eyebrows also contributes to achieving hunter eyes.

 Here is an example showing you the minimum and ideal length:

[align=center][/align]

 [size=22][b]The [color=#475577]Inner Length[/color][/b][/size]

 The inner part of your eyebrows should be [b]almost parellel to your nosedrills[/b]. Too much gap between them looks feminine. Having too less space shows that you don't take care of yourself.

 [size=22][b]The[color=#475577] Set [/color][/b](optional)[/size]

 [b]The closer your eyebrows are set to your eyes the better.[/b] There are only a few ways to change the set beside surgery, I'll name them later in "The Growth" section. However having [u]high set eyebrows is definitely not a death sentence[/u], you can be good looking with high set eyebrows, but you will be lacking the alpha/slayer look, because of the increased vertical length of your eye area.

