 [size=22][b]The [color=#475577]Tilt[/color][/b][/size]

[align=center][/align]

 This is something that many people don't even notice. Negative tilted eyebrows causes your whole eye area to look beta. [b]The ideal is either neutral or positive tilted[/b]. What fits you better will depend on the set of your eyebrows, the canthal tilt of your eyes, tissue length, jaw angularity and harmony in general. For instance, if you have negative tilted eyes, positive tilted eyebrows can balance out your eye area. High set eyebrows don't go too well with a positive tilt, since it makes your eye area even taller. 'Hunter' eyebrows can be achieved with both neutral and negative tilted eyebrows, but they need to be low set in the first place.

 [size=22][b]The [color=#475577]Density[/color][/b]

 [size=15]There's not much to say here. Everyone should know that eyebrows with [b]low density make you less attractive[/b]. [/size] [/size]

